Subject: [PATCH] rockchip: nanopi-r76s: use HS200 for eMMC in U-Boot

Select HS200 in the board's U-Boot and SPL configurations and advertise
it in the U-Boot device tree. The Linux device tree retains HS400.

Reference: https://github.com/sbwml/package_boot_uboot-rockchip/blob/f4e9bc7b649d80e8b01fd493918999ffffc1cac2/patches/900-board-rockchip-Add-support-for-FriendlyARM-NanoPi-R7.patch
---
diff --git a/arch/arm/dts/rk3576-nanopi-r76s-u-boot.dtsi b/arch/arm/dts/rk3576-nanopi-r76s-u-boot.dtsi
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/arch/arm/dts/rk3576-nanopi-r76s-u-boot.dtsi
@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
+
+#include "rk3576-u-boot.dtsi"
+
+&sdhci {
+	/delete-property/ mmc-hs400-1_8v;
+	/delete-property/ mmc-hs400-enhanced-strobe;
+	mmc-hs200-1_8v;
+};
diff --git a/configs/nanopi-r76s-rk3576_defconfig b/configs/nanopi-r76s-rk3576_defconfig
--- a/configs/nanopi-r76s-rk3576_defconfig
+++ b/configs/nanopi-r76s-rk3576_defconfig
@@ -38,4 +38,6 @@
 CONFIG_SUPPORT_EMMC_RPMB=y
+CONFIG_MMC_HS200_SUPPORT=y
+CONFIG_SPL_MMC_HS200_SUPPORT=y
 CONFIG_MMC_DW=y
 CONFIG_MMC_DW_ROCKCHIP=y
 CONFIG_MMC_SDHCI=y
